    "body": "Quick pass (coordinator, read only, no build) on head `9ca89a5ce`: the PR merges cleanly with `main`. It changes `xtask`, the `gate` skill, site files and one decision file. It changes no file in `.github/`, no workflow trigger and no runner. The body has `Process change: yes`, the state of the site tests before and after, the rule for a missing tool, what the runners need, the pins, what was not exercised, and `Fixes #4133`; `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` is not changed. The writer record on #4133 is released. The PR is flagged ready. It waits for the independent review. The maintainer decides the merge; the coordinator does not merge this PR.\n\nNotes for the reviewer:\n- The site tests were red on `main` `39298012` (112 tests, 23 failures) and are green on this head (112, OK). Check that the site fixes agree with the shipped app, and that no site test is weaker.\n- The new step is not a cargo step (`xtask/src/site_step.rs`, `exec.rs`). It runs in the batch tier and the release tier, and in the quick tier when the diff touches an input. The pin `each_path_that_a_site_test_names_is_an_input` holds the input list against the paths that the site tests open.\n- A missing tool (python 3, zola, node): a `SKIP` row in quick and batch (\"not a pass\"), a `FAIL` row in the release tier. Check that a skipped site step can never read as `ok`.\n- The cut runner needs python 3, zola 0.23.6 and node on its PATH before the next cut, or the cut gate is red at the site step. The post-merge runner needs the same tools, or the step is a `SKIP` row there. The body has the details for the maintainer. Follow-up: #4433.\n- The PR also changes `xtask/src/unit_sweep.rs` (a clippy finding on Rust 1.100). Check that the logic is the same on each OS.",
